  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Quasi stationary high pres sprawling across the\nMid- Atlantic and low pressure well off the FL coast will \nresult in cont northeasterly flow across the region today. The \nhigh waves combined with King Tides this week will lead to \nadditional minor coastal flooding impacts on the OBX.\n\nMinor coastal flooding of vulnerable locations still possible \nthrough today with \"sunny day\" flooding across much of the \ntidal regions of coastal ENC around times of high tide. Coastal\nflood advisories continue through the high tide cycle today to\naccount for these elevated water levels. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Hts/thicknesses build further to round out the\nweek and temps climbing back to ~10 degrees above climo with \nhighs upr 70s to near 80 inland to low 70s OBX through Friday. A\nreinforcing back door cool front will bring temps down closer to\nclimo (low 70s most locales) on Sunday. Low temps will also\nremain above normal through much of the period with readings in\nthe 50s. Normal lows for most of the FA are in the 45-50 range\nnow.  \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...High pres ridge finally begins to break down by\nTuesday and esp Wednesday as next potential low pres area and\ncold front make it's way into the region on active sub tropical\njet. Still timing differences on latest 29/00Z model suite, but\nit appears this system could bring beneficial widespread rain to\nthe area. For now, due to timing differences, pops are in the\n30-40% range at this time for the mid week period.",
